Node.js has released <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v0.10.42/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v0.10.42 (Maintenance)</a>, <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v0.12.10/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v0.12.10 (LTS)</a>, <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v4.4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v4.4.0 (LTS)</a>, and <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v5.8.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v5.8.0 (Stable)</a>. These versions include vulnerability fixes and updates to OpenSSL.

For more details, see the <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/february-2016-security-releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">summary of security releases</a>.

